  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Access to Basic Needs, Protection and Transportation Services for Refugees in Jordan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refugees account for almost 10 per cent of Jordan&apos;s population. There are 670,748 registered Syrian refugees and roughly 90,000 registered refugees of other nationalities, primarily from Iraq, Yemen, and Sudan in Jordan. The vast majority (83%) reside outside camps in urban areas. To address priority needs identified in coordination with partners and building on previous support, IOM plans to continue with the provision of basic needs assistance through multi-purpose cash assistance and winter cash assistance to the most vulnerable refugees in Jordan, while identifying households/individuals with specific, complex, or multiple vulnerabilities, and through the provision of integrated case management effectively assist them to address their protection needs.</narrative>
  </description>
